-/// Handles did change text document notifications
-/// Edits are applied to `curr_doc` and `tree`, but `tree` is not
-/// re-parsed
+/// Handles did change text document notifications.
+///
+/// The whole document is re-parsed instead of applying the incremental
+/// `content_changes` to the stored tree with `Tree::edit`.
+///
+/// `text_doc_change_to_ts_edit` computes the edit's byte offsets against the
+/// *already updated* document, while LSP ranges refer to the document as it
+/// was before the change. For edits that span lines and insert text with
+/// newlines, the resulting `InputEdit` therefore does not describe the tree
+/// it is applied to. The tree then contains nodes past the end of the new
+/// text and the next request panics in `Node::utf8_text` with
+/// `range end index N out of range for slice of length M`, which takes the
+/// whole language server down.
+///
+/// Assembly buffers are small, so a full re-parse is cheap and always leaves
+/// the tree consistent with the document text.
 ///
 /// # Errors
 ///
